{
  "_note": "介入風格預設 (plan §11 Phase 2). A style is a NAMED BUNDLE OF SETTINGS THAT ALREADY EXIST - it adds no new engine behaviour. It is keyed by ALGORITHM, never by edge id, so one style works on any scene: a scene names its own edges (phrase_modx, iridium_to_wavestate) and a style that referenced them would only ever fit one rig. Applying a style stashes what was there first, so 取消風格 puts it all back. Every value here is a STARTING POINT chosen from what the machinery supports, not a claim about how the music should sound - play each one and move the sliders.",
  "_tension": "0 = chord tones only. 0.35+ adds the diatonic 9/11/13. 0.70+ any natural extension. 0.85+ the altered tones (b9 #9 #11 b13).",
  "_time": "one knob stretching or compressing every wait in the scene: echo delays, how long a pad holds, how much silence a lane wants before entering. It QUANTISES to musical ratios (1/4 1/3 1/2 2/3 1 1.5 2 3 4), so write a value that IS one of them - 1.8 lands on 2 and 0.85 lands on 1, and a style that meant to be slower or tighter would then do nothing and say nothing.",
  "_density": "how thick the engine's answer is; it scales how many notes a lane offers.",
